  "published": "2026-09-25T23:06:06.793Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes interop calls throwing on a slider that has left the DOM. When a swiper-container is removed, its disconnectedCallback destroys the Swiper, and Swiper's destroy strips every property of the instance but clears .swiper only on the inner shadow element - so the host keeps pointing at a gutted instance, and a late SlideTo failed with \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'cssMode')\". Every interop entry point now treats a destroyed instance as no slider at all, and deferred work - the auto-height observers, the resize re-anchor, the anchor observer, awaited thumbs/controller selectors and event forwarding - checks that the instance it was set up for is still the live one before acting on it, so it neither throws on a destroyed slider nor moves a replaced one. Same vendored Swiper 14.0.6 bundle.",
